 "result": "I documented 12 repos this run, hit the cap, and pushed one docs commit to each. All pushes went through and I reached every repo.\n\nFive were backfills, the new 2026-11-27 repos: sodashelf, whatareyou, lumbricus, familytree and parallaxwire. The other seven were updates: rocketbench, ghostwing, hopper, field-twin, cliprig, manualrebuild and ascend. I also pushed the refreshed profile README to the sudosilo repo, and committed `scribe/state.json`, `scribe/repos.json`, `scribe/publish.json` and the notes to control-troll main as \"scribe state\".\n\nNo backfills remain. About 16 repos still have real changes waiting for the next run. The biggest are hubview, with 189 commits since the last run, and mohavetech-website, with 47 bot sync commits. The others are itchy-troll, the testbed, blue-agent, downfree-foundry, scores, shared-server, fleetindex, filecensus, birdix, final-vector, rogue-rail, artifactium, centipede and pajamastan-space-administration.\n\nOver 100 more repos only have footer seal commits or developer README cleanups. I left them untouched, since they change nothing a user sees and only need a lastSha refresh.\n\nNone of the new repos needed a root `vercel.json` change. Only parallaxwire is live at its own address. The `.vercel.app` names for whatareyou, lumbricus and familytree answer 200 but serve a different page, so I gave those no homepage.\n\nThe release and repo-setting jobs are queued in `publish.json` for the scribe-publish workflow; I haven't confirmed that workflow ran.\n\n`agents/notes/general.md` is now well over 40 lines. I added three notes and did not condense it.",
